// ============================================================
//  SMART CAMPUS EMERGENCY ROUTE MANAGER  (C++ console project)
//
//  User-implemented data structures (no STL containers):
//    1. Linked list   -> adjacency list of the campus graph (EdgeNode)
//    2. Stack (array) -> undo the last blocked path
//    3. Queue (array) -> BFS to find cut-off locations
//    4. Sorted linked list (priority queue) -> incidents by severity
//
//  Algorithms: Dijkstra's shortest path, BFS
//
//  <sstream>  : reads a whole line and splits it into words, so
//               "main gate", "MAIN_GATE" and "Main_Gate" all work.
//  File handling:
//      campus_data.txt  -> map, blocked paths, hazards, pending incidents
//                          (saved after every change, loaded at start)
//      incident_log.txt -> history of every incident that was handled
// ============================================================
